  "rawBulletin": "India Meteorological Department\n(Ministry of Earth Sciences)\nNATIONAL BULLETIN NO. 25 (BOB/09/2026)\nTIME OF ISSUE: 2330 HOURS IST DATED: 03.11.2026\nFROM: INDIA METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (FAX NO. 24643965/24699216/24623220)\nTO: CONTROL ROOM, NDM, MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS (FAX.NO. 23093750)\nCONTROL ROOM NDMA (FAX.NO. 26701729)\nCABINET SECRETARIAT (FAX.NO.23012284, 23018638)\nPS TO HON\u2019BLE MINISTER FOR S & T AND EARTH SCIENCES (FAX NO.23316745)\nSECRETARY, MOES (FAX NO. 24629777)\nH.Q. (INTEGRATED DEFENCE STAFF AND CDS) (FAX NO. 23005137/23005147)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, DOORDARSHAN (23385843)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, AIR (23421105, 23421219)\nPIB MOES (FAX NO. 23389042)\nUNI (FAX NO. 23355841)\nD.G. NATIONAL DISASTER RESPONSE FORCE (NDRF) (FAX NO. 26105912, 2436 3260)\nDIRECTOR, PUNCTUALITY, INDIAN RAILWAYS (FAX NO. 23388503)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDAMAN & NICOBAR ISLANDS (FAX NO. 03192-232656)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDHRA PRADESH (FAX NO. 0863-2441029)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ODISHA (FAX NO. 0674-2536660)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF TAMIL NADU (FAX NO. 044-25672304)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF PUDUCHERRY (FAX NO. 0413-2334145)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF WEST BENGAL (FAX NO. 033-22144328)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF TELANGANA (FAX NO. 40-23455340)\nSub: - Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu] weakened into a Deep Depression over\nCoastal Andhra Pradesh\nThe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu]\u201d over south coastal Andhra Pradesh moved\nnorth-northwestwards with a speed of 07 kmph during past 06 hours, weakened into a Deep Depression\nand lay centered at 2030 hours IST of today the 03rd November, 2026 over the Coastal Andhra Pradesh,\nnear Latitude 16.3\u00b0N and Longitude 80.0\u00b0E, about 60 km south-southwest of Nandigama (Andhra\nPradesh), 70 km west-southwest of Vijayawada (Andhra Pradesh), 110 km southeast of Nalgonda\n(Telangana), 110 km south of Khammam (Telangana) and 180 km south-southwest of Bhadrachalam\n(Telangana).\nThe maximum sustained wind speed was 55-65 gusting to 75 kmph at 2030 hrs IST of today, the 3rd\nNovember 2026.\nContinuing to move nearly north-northwestwards, it is likely to weaken into a depression (wind speed\nreaching 40-50 kmph gusting to 60 kmph) by morning of tomorrow, the 4th November, 2026.\nIt is under the continuous surveillance of Doppler Weather Radars at Machilipatnam and Visakhapatnam.\n.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(IST) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n03.11.26/2030 16.3/80.0 55-65 gusting to 75 Deep Depression\n03.11.26/2330 16.5/80.0 55-65 gusting to 75 Deep Depression\n04.11.26/0530 16.8 /80.0 40-50 gusting to 60 Depression\n(i) Rainfall warning:\nCoastal Andhra Pradesh: Light to moderate rainfall at most places with heavy to very heavy rainfall at\na few places and extremely heavy rainfall at isolated places on 03rd November, and heavy to very heavy\nrainfall at isolated places on 4th November.\nNorth Tamil Nadu: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at isolated places on\n3rd November.\nSouth Odisha: Light to moderate rainfall at few places with heavy rainfall at isolated places on 3rd\nNovember.\nRayalaseema: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy at isolated places on 3rd November.\nTelangana: Light to Moderate rainfall at most places with heavy to very heavy at a few places and\nextremely heavy rainfall at isolated places over Eastern Telangana on 03rd November. Isolated heavy\nrainfall is also likely over northeast Telangana on 4th November, 2026.\nChhattisgarh: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at isolated places 3rd -4th\nNovember.\n(ii) Wind warnings:\n\u2756 Westcentral Bay of Bengal:\nSqually wind speeds reaching 50-60 kmph gusting to 70 kmph would prevail till midnight of 3rd and\ndecrease gradually becoming 40-50 gusting to 60 kmph by 4th morning and improve thereafter.\n\u2756 Coastal Andhra Pradesh (Krishna, Bapatla, Prakasham, SPSR Nell",
